1. while loop
while (true) {
    System.out.println("Infinite while loop");
}

👉 Condition is always true, so it never stops.

2. do-while loop
do {
    System.out.println("Infinite do-while loop");
} while (true);

👉 Runs at least once, then continues forever because condition is true.

3. for loop
for (;;) {
    System.out.println("Infinite for loop");
}

👉 No initialization, condition, or update → loop runs infinitely.
